  "result": "Completion now handles arguments that contain `#`. The shell completion tests pass (59), including a new one for this case.\n\nThe cause was in `split_arg_string` in `src/click/shell_completion.py`. It uses `shlex`, which treats `#` as the start of a comment by default. Everything from the `#` onward was dropped before completion ran. I set `lex.commenters = \"\"` so `#` is kept as an ordinary character.\n\nI added `test_split_arg_string_hash` to `tests/test_shell_completion.py`. I didn't add a `CHANGES.md` entry, because the top section there is the already-released 8.5.0.",
